# Unit21
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit21核心词汇

impress/ɪmˈpres/给…留下印象/Her speech impressed the audience greatly.
improve/ɪmˈpruːv/改善/You need to improve your English skills.
incident/ˈɪnsɪdənt/事件/The police investigated the incident.
include/ɪnˈkluːd/包括/The price includes breakfast and dinner.
income/ˈɪnkʌm/收入/His monthly income is about 10,000 yuan.
increase/ɪnˈkriːs/增加/Prices have increased by 10% this year.
incredible/ɪnˈkredəbl/难以置信的/The view from the top is incredible.
indeed/ɪnˈdiːd/确实/She is indeed a talented singer.
independent/ˌɪndɪˈpendənt/独立的/She is an independent and confident woman.
indicate/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/表明；指示/The data indicates a clear trend.
individual/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl/个人的/Each individual has different needs.
industry/ˈɪndəstri/工业；行业/The tourism industry is growing rapidly.
influence/ˈɪnfluəns/影响/Parents have a great influence on their children.
inform/ɪnˈfɔːrm/通知/Please inform me of any changes.
initial/ɪˈnɪʃl/最初的/His initial reaction was surprise.
injure/ˈɪndʒər/受伤/He was seriously injured in the accident.
inner/ˈɪnər/内部的/She kept her feelings to her inner self.
innocent/ˈɪnəsənt/无辜的；天真的/He was proved innocent of the crime.
input/ˈɪnpʊt/投入；输入/We need more input from the team.
inquiry/ɪnˈkwaɪəri/询问；调查/The police made an inquiry into the matter.
insist/ɪnˈsɪst/坚持/He insisted on paying for dinner.
inspect/ɪnˈspekt/检查/The officer inspected the building for safety.
inspire/ɪnˈspaɪər/激励/Her story inspired many young people.
install/ɪnˈstɔːl/安装/They installed a new air conditioner.
instance/ˈɪnstəns/实例/For instance, you can use this method.
instead/ɪnˈsted/代替/He didn't go to the party; instead, he stayed home.
instinct/ˈɪnstɪŋkt/本能/Animals rely on instinct to survive.
institution/ˌɪnstɪˈtuːʃn/机构/Universities are important educational institutions.
instruct/ɪnˈstrʌkt/指示；教授/The teacher instructed the students to finish the work.
instrument/ˈɪnstrəmənt/仪器；乐器/She plays several musical instruments.
insurance/ɪnˈʃʊrəns/保险/Health insurance is very important.
intellectual/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl/知识分子的/He is an intellectual with wide interests.
intelligence/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns/智力；情报/Artificial intelligence is developing rapidly.
intend/ɪnˈtend/打算/I intend to travel abroad next year.
intense/ɪnˈtens/强烈的/The competition is very intense.
interest/ˈɪntrəst/兴趣/She has a strong interest in science.
interfere/ˌɪntərˈfɪr/干涉/Don't interfere in other people's affairs.
internal/ɪnˈtɜːrnl/内部的/The company solved its internal problems.
international/ˌɪntərˈnæʃnəl/国际的/International trade is very important.
interpret/ɪnˈtɜːrprɪt/解释；口译/She works as an interpreter at the conference.
interrupt/ˌɪntəˈrʌpt/打断/It's rude to interrupt someone while they're speaking.
interview/ˈɪntərvjuː/面试；采访/She has a job interview tomorrow.
introduce/ˌɪntrəˈduːs/介绍/Let me introduce my colleague to you.
invade/ɪnˈveɪd/入侵/The army invaded the neighboring country.
invest/ɪnˈvest/投资/He invested a lot of money in the stock market.
investigate/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt/调查/The police are investigating the crime.
investigation/ɪnˌvestɪˈɡeɪʃn/调查/The investigation revealed the truth.
invisible/ɪnˈvɪzəbl/看不见的/Germs are invisible to the naked eye.
invite/ɪnˈvaɪt/邀请/She invited me to her birthday party.
involve/ɪnˈvɑːlv/涉及；参与/The project involves a lot of teamwork.
